  "name": "Question 20",
  "problem": "The building model has the same ratio of length to width as a real building\nThe following table shows the length and width of the building model in centimeters. \n\n| Length | Width |\n| --- | --- |\n| $84$ | $41$ |\n\nBy rounding the given data to the nearest ten, approximate the length of the building if it is known that its width is $20$ meters.",
  "worked_solution": "First, let's round the length and width of the building model:\n\n- Length: $84⟶80$\n\n- Width: $41⟶40$\n\nTherefore, the ratio of the length to the width (expressed as a fraction) is approximately\n\n$$\n\\frac{80}{40}.\n$$\n\nSo the numerator represents the length of the building model, and the denominator represents the width.\n\nWe can simplify this ratio by dividing both numbers by $10$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{80÷10}{40÷10}=\\frac{8}{4}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide by $4$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{8÷4}{4÷4}=\\frac{2}{1}\n$$\n\nWe can make a denominator of $20$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $20$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{2\\times 20}{1\\times 20}=\\frac{40}{20}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the length of the building is approximately $40$ meters.",
